What is the product $x_1 \\cdot x_2$?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$-15$"},{"key":"B","text":"$-2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$15$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'Substituting $y = x + 2$ into $x^2 + y^2 = 34$ gives $x^2 + (x + 2)^2 = 34$, which expands to $x^2 + x^2 + 4x + 4 = 34$, or $2x^2 + 4x - 30 = 0$. Dividing by $2$: $x^2 + 2x - 15 = 0$, which factors as $(x + 5)(x - 3) = 0$. The solutions are $x = -5$ and $x = 3$, so the product is $(-5)(3) = -15$. The distractor $-2$ is the sum of the $x$-values rather than the product. The distractor $2$ results from a sign error when computing the sum. The distractor $15$ results from dropping the negative sign on the product.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 105, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);











