$$\\begin{cases} 2x + y = 19 \\\\ x - y = 2 \\end{cases}$$', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$(7, 5)$"},{"key":"B","text":"$(5, 7)$"},{"key":"C","text":"$(7, -5)$"},{"key":"D","text":"$(10, -1)$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'Adding the two equations eliminates $y$: $(2x + y) + (x - y) = 19 + 2$, giving $3x = 21$ and $x = 7$. Substituting $x = 7$ into $x - y = 2$ gives $7 - y = 2$, so $y = 5$. The solution is $(7, 5)$. The pair $(5, 7)$ reverses the $x$- and $y$-values and satisfies neither equation. The pair $(7, -5)$ has the correct $x$-value but a sign error on $y$. The pair $(10, -1)$ satisfies the first equation ($2(10) + (-1) = 19$) but not the second ($10 - (-1) = 11 \\neq 2$), resulting from checking only one equation.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 60, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);




Yet a close examination of Aidoo''s private correspondence from the 1970s reveals that she was equally influenced by European modernist techniques, particularly the stream-of-consciousness methods of Virginia Woolf. This complicates Kwarteng''s framework by suggesting that Aidoo''s formal experiments arise from a convergence of traditions rather than a single cultural source.', $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"It qualifies the argument presented in the first paragraph by introducing evidence that suggests a more complex explanation."},{"key":"B","text":"It refutes the first paragraph's central claim by demonstrating that the claim is based on a factual error."},{"key":"C","text":"It provides additional support for the first paragraph's argument by citing a new primary source."},{"key":"D","text":"It shifts to a different topic by examining the broader influence of European modernism on African literature."}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'A', NULL, E'The second paragraph introduces Aidoo''s correspondence showing European modernist influence, which complicates rather than overturns Kwarteng''s claim — suggesting the explanation is more complex than a single cultural source. This qualifies, not refutes, the first paragraph''s argument, since no factual error is identified. The correspondence does not support Kwarteng''s claim; it introduces an alternative influence. The paragraph remains focused on Aidoo''s specific formal choices, not on European modernism''s broader influence on African literature as a whole.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"inference_overreach"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"detail_misread"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 90, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date